OpenPyCharm Notebooks
Copyright OpenPyCharm contributors

This independent implementation uses the public Apache-2.0 IntelliJ Platform
and open-source PythonCore APIs. No proprietary notebook implementation is
included. Notebook persistence implements the public nbformat v4 specification.

The optional runtime dependencies jupyter_client and ipykernel are separately
installed in the user's selected interpreter. Their BSD-3-Clause licenses and
their dependencies' notices remain in those packages; no dependency source is
vendored in this plugin. The kernel requirements are pinned separately.

Public specifications and APIs:
https://nbformat.readthedocs.io/en/stable/format_description.html
https://jupyter-client.readthedocs.io/en/stable/api/client.html
https://jupyter-client.readthedocs.io/en/stable/messaging.html
https://github.com/JetBrains/intellij-community/tree/456919a9624bae72ac12efafc35d2b916cb0c5c5/platform/editor-ui-api/src/com/intellij/openapi/fileEditor

Static Markdown preview uses the existing Apache-2.0 JetBrains markdown library
from the authenticated open-source SDK, without vendoring or replacing it:
https://github.com/JetBrains/markdown
Pinned SDK lib/intellij.libraries.markdown.jar SHA-256:
74b475effd0b3b622aa9d20fbbfd168fb4e61e218124989ccffcfa51a680f5dd
Its upstream notices remain in the SDK/product distribution.

Images use Java ImageIO with memory-only input streams. HTML is converted to
inert Swing text/table data; no browser, script engine or URL loader is used.
Matplotlib, pandas and Pillow used by the rich-output tests are external
test-producer packages, never bundled IDE implementation.
